RESULT round 2: 8 of 8 killed, 0 survived.
- status-line and sgr-prefix (B2): killed by interactive_transparency (the drawn bytes are not exactly the bytes the
  server sent plus ESC[0m).
- shared-default-label (B1, the default label back to "cli"): the second default attach is ready on the holder's lease
  and never exits (interactive_owners test 1), and the operator's detach no longer releases the interact lease while the
  observer of the same owner remains (interactive_attach observer test).
- observer-reads-geometry: killed by interactive_owners test 2 (see the correction below).

## Correction of round 1

Round 1 recorded `observer-resizes` (`plan.observe && false` in attach/session.rs) as SURVIVED and called it
equivalent. That was wrong. When the observer shares its operator's client label (round 1: the shared default `cli`),
the mutated observer reads the owner's geometry lease (open.rs::geometry_lease matches the holder label; the server
matches the lease by owner principal), and its grid reached the program (gate probe observer_grid_reached_program=true).
It has the same root cause as B1. Round 2 kills it with
interactive_owners::an_observer_sharing_its_operators_label_never_claims_the_owners_geometry_or_input: the observer's
33x11 grid reaches the program, and its detach record lists the owner's interact-role lease.

